{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786911632505},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the task:\n1. I need to use two datasets:\n   - US farmers markets by state (2026): https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n   - 2025 population census data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\n2. I need to:\n   - Get total farmers markets (excluding territories)\n   - Get 2025 population from the 'United States' row in the census file\n   - Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n   - Report to 4 decimal places\n   - Verify everything using the tools\n\n3. According to the instructions, I should:\n   - First check if there's a catalog with semantic models\n   - Orient by checking catalog_list_aliases and semantic_models\n   - If no existing alias covers this, ingest the data\n   - Use xorq_select to get values\n   - Use xorq_verify to verify the answer\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog path. The default is `.xorq/catalog`.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the catalog and then ingesting the data as needed."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01MJQ56Z7c5TJcmzVmcbZhiK","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01RDhWew4r4FXmrCYkih9gpf","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01F6Sq5qbP5bYjKKoFxxruzA","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":483,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8181,"totalTokens":8674,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.002415,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01022625,"total":0.01265125},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":288},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911632528,"responseId":"msg_011Ce73kMGFpynQgkWqXzKVo","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01MJQ56Z7c5TJcmzVmcbZhiK","toolName":"xorq_catalog_info","content":[{"type":"text","text":"path:    /private/tmp/trial-pi-9-w1a_5at7/.xorq/catalog\ncommit:  0fab8e797d93\nremotes: (none)\nentries: 0\naliases: 0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911637668},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01RDhWew4r4FXmrCYkih9gpf","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911637669},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01F6Sq5qbP5bYjKKoFxxruzA","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911637669},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest the data. According to the project instructions, I should:\n1. Create build scripts in `.xorq/scripts/` \n2. Use `xo.deferred_read_csv()` to read the data\n3. Build and add to the catalog\n\nLet me create the build scripts for both datasets.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I'll need to ingest both datasets. Let me create the build scripts:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Adz1mH5C25Ckz